# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit .env.
#
# Configuration keys nest with a double underscore: Email:MailerSend:ApiToken
# is Email__MailerSend__ApiToken.

# ── Email ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave the whole section unset for local development. A Development host with
# no provider configured captures messages to the console — links included —
# and delivers nothing, so the application runs with no credentials at all.
#
# Outside Development, a missing provider or a missing credential stops the
# application at startup rather than letting it run and drop mail silently.
# See src/Sw5e.Email/README.md for every key.

# MailerSend | Smtp | Capture
#Email__Provider=MailerSend
#Email__FromAddress=noreply@example.com
#Email__FromName=SW5e
#Email__ReplyToAddress=support@example.com

# SECRET. Issued per sending domain in the MailerSend dashboard. Never commit a
# real value here or anywhere else.
#Email__MailerSend__ApiToken=

# Generic SMTP relay, used when Email__Provider=Smtp. Port 587 with STARTTLS;
# port 465 is not supported and is rejected at startup.
#Email__Smtp__Host=smtp.example.com
#Email__Smtp__Port=587
#Email__Smtp__UserName=
# SECRET. Same rules as the API token.
#Email__Smtp__Password=
